# Prototype skills in selected NAV advertisements

Included: 13 distinct validated model extractions. Excluded: 0 (0 blocked, 0 failed, 0 stale, 0 pending).

Activity at last saved check among included ads: 8 ACTIVE, 5 INACTIVE, 0 UNKNOWN. These are not live status checks. All included ads contribute to the historical counts; no active-only table is produced.

This is a small-sample prototype, not complete Innlandet market coverage or manually approved extraction ground truth. Some selected extractions have known interpretation warnings.

## Saved publication dates and coverage

Publication date available for 13 of 13 selected ads (0 missing, 0 invalid). Their saved publication dates span 2025-11-27 through 2026-11-03.

These are dates among selected ads, not the period covered by NAV collection. An older publication date on an updated ad does not establish historical collection coverage. No weekly, monthly or yearly statistics are calculated.

## Counting rules

- Saved skill names are used except for explicit version-checked provisional corrections. No aliases or similar names are merged.
- Each UUID counts once per skill and classification. Total is the union of UUIDs, so it can be smaller than the sum of the three classification columns.
- The main table counts only single applicant qualifications. A duty, team practice or interest does not become an applicant requirement.
- OR choices are listed as groups, not as independently required skills. The saved order is preserved; each exact group counts once per UUID and classification.
- Duties, work context and interest-only single mentions are counted separately below. Their counts describe mentions, not applicant demand.
- Rows and category totals can overlap; do not add rows to obtain a number of unique ads.

## Review basis

Applied 24 item corrections from `reviews/current-v2.json`. Original run files are unchanged. Review decisions and unresolved cases are in the review file. These are provisional, not approved ground truth.

An `unclear` mention is not evidence of applicant demand. A named OR alternative is not independently mandatory.

